{"assets":["/statement-assets/f972ea49575a31a1707db1c1197bcbe2f7fec813c316f50b3631300c2372f5d9.png","/statement-assets/23c7da2a1c81cd3314efdbcffebf79c3c4d0423280507082b0da62af69d32624.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"526","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Transmitting Levels"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Optimizing the amount of data transmitted via a network is an important and interesting part of developing any network application."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f972ea49575a31a1707db1c1197bcbe2f7fec813c316f50b3631300c2372f5d9.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one secret game developed deep in the ZeptoLab company, the game universe consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" levels, located in a circle. You can get from level "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" to levels "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", also you can get from level "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to level "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and vice versa. The map of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th level description size is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" bytes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In order to reduce the transmitted traffic, the game gets levels as follows. All the levels on the server are divided into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" groups and each time a player finds himself on one of the levels of a certain group for the first time, the server sends all levels of the group to the game client as a single packet. Thus, when a player travels inside the levels of a single group, the application doesn't need any new information. Due to the technical limitations the packet can contain an arbitrary number of levels but their total size mustn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" bytes, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" is some positive integer constant."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Usual situation is that players finish levels one by one, that's why a decision was made to split "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" levels into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" groups so that each group was a continuous segment containing multiple neighboring levels (also, the group can have two adjacent levels, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Specifically, if the descriptions of all levels have the total weight of at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" bytes, then they can all be united into one group to be sent in a single packet."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine, what minimum number of groups do you need to make in order to organize the levels of the game observing the conditions above?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As developing a game is a long process and technology never stagnates, it is yet impossible to predict exactly what value will take constant value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" limiting the packet size when the game is out. That's why the developers ask you to find the answer for multiple values of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ q ≤ 50"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of levels in the game universe and the number of distinct values of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" that you need to process."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the sizes of the levels in bytes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/23c7da2a1c81cd3314efdbcffebf79c3c4d0423280507082b0da62af69d32624.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"), determining the values of constant "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":", for which you need to determine the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"kj"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the input print on a single line integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"mj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ mj ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), determining the minimum number of groups to divide game levels into for transmission via network observing the given conditions. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 3\n2 4 2 1 3 2\n7\n4\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n4\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the test from the statement you can do in the following manner."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" at "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b = 7"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can divide into two segments: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2|421|32"},{"kind":"text","text":" (note that one of the segments contains the fifth, sixth and first levels); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" at "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b = 4"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can divide into four segments: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2|4|21|3|2"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" at "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b = 6"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can divide into three segments: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"24|21|32|"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"526E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/526/problem/E"}